// A `for ... by` over 100,000 entities: built --parallel their keys are
// sorted on many threads (from 16,384 on), by the same passes, so in the
// same order as on one: those alike in the order they are stored, those
// below nought first. The order, as a hash of who came when, the same
// both ways, each time.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/ordered_parallel.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/ordered_parallel.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// CHECK:      step 0: 100000 rows, order 5796329773731977640
// CHECK-NEXT: step 1: 100000 rows, order 3085602959123592563
// CHECK:      step 4: 100000 rows, order 6974316037733467605
